verdict.answer:
A Member State may exempt these vehicles from the driving time, break and rest rules (Articles 5 to 9), provided the objectives of the Regulation are not prejudiced. The exemption applies on its own territory, or on another Member State's territory if the States concerned agree. It can be made subject to individual conditions. The conditions for postal vehicles are:
- the vehicle or combination has a maximum permissible mass not exceeding 7,5 tonnes;
- it is used by a universal service provider to deliver items as part of the universal service;
- it is used only within a 100 km radius of the undertaking's base;
- driving is not the driver's main activity.
The exemption is not automatic: each Member State decides whether to grant it and must inform the Commission.
